{
  "_comment": [
    "Golden signal-packing vectors, derived from the DBC/Vector bit-numbering",
    "convention that tools/dbc2boatjson.py copies verbatim into StartPos (see",
    "docs/howto/dbc2boatjson.md). These are hand-derived from the convention,",
    "NOT captured from any implementation -- that is the point: they are the",
    "spec, so an implementation that disagrees is the thing that is wrong.",
    "",
    "For ByteOrder 1 (Motorola) StartPos is the MSB position: bit index n",
    "addresses byte n // 8, bit n % 8, and bits run downward, wrapping to the",
    "next byte's bit 7. There is no 7 - (n % 8) inversion.",
    "",
    "The C++ COM library (src/hil/pdu/com/com_signal.cpp) does NOT currently",
    "satisfy this table for Motorola -- see the backlog item. When it is fixed",
    "it should be made to read these same rows."
  ],
